From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: don't start the GPU before its zap shader exists

The Retroid Pocket Duo's zap shader is signed for the device, so PB-OS ships
none; rpduo-firmware copies it from the Duo's own Android partitions once
the root file system is up (about 8 s into boot). The in-kernel fbdev client
opens the DRM device at about 0.45 s, msm_open() then loads the GPU, and the
zap is not there yet: hw init fails with -ENOENT and leaves the GMU stuck, so
every later open (gamescope) fails with "Timeout waiting for GMU OOB set
GPU_SET" and -ETIMEDOUT, and Vulkan finds no GPU.

adreno_load_gpu() already returns early, without touching the hardware,
when the GPU's other firmware is missing ("the number one reason for HW init
to fail"). Do the same when the zap-shader node names a firmware file that
can't be loaded yet. load_gpu() retries on every open, so the first open
after rpduo-firmware has run starts the GPU. Devices whose zap is already
on the firmware path are not affected.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -65,6 +65,36 @@
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A device-specific zap shader (zap-shader/firmware-name) may only reach the
+ * firmware search path after boot: the Retroid Pocket Duo's is copied from
+ * its own Android partitions by userspace. The in-kernel fbdev client opens
+ * the device long before that, and a first hw init without the zap leaves
+ * the GMU stuck, so every later open fails too ("Timeout waiting for GMU OOB
+ * set GPU_SET"). Don't power the GPU up until the zap can be loaded; the
+ * next open tries again.
+ */
+static bool adreno_zap_fw_ready(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	const struct firmware *fw;
+	struct device_node *np;
+	const char *name = NULL;
+	bool ready = true;
+
+	np = of_get_available_child_by_name(pdev->dev.of_node, "zap-shader");
+	if (!np)
+		return true;
+	of_property_read_string_index(np, "firmware-name", 0, &name);
+	if (name) {
+		if (request_firmware_direct(&fw, name, &pdev->dev))
+			ready = false;
+		else
+			release_firmware(fw);
+	}
+	of_node_put(np);
+	return ready;
+}
+
 struct msm_gpu *adreno_load_gpu(struct drm_device *dev)
 {
 	struct msm_drm_private *priv = dev->dev_private;
@@ -97,6 +127,11 @@
 		ret = gpu->funcs->ucode_load(gpu);
 		if (ret)
 			return NULL;
+	}
+
+	if (!adreno_zap_fw_ready(pdev)) {
+		dev_info(dev->dev, "zap shader not available yet, GPU start waits for the next open\n");
+		return NULL;
 	}
 
 	/*
